    {
        "content": "<p>Having oriented matroids in mathlib would be great in light of the <a href=\"#narrow/channel/116395-maths/topic/Polyhedra.20in.20mathlib/with/573982556\">polyhedral theory</a> that we are PR-ing piece-by-piece at the moment. This would be the right language to formulate various theorems about polyhedra/polytopes.</p>",
        "id": 578213318,
        "sender_full_name": "Martin Winter",
        "timestamp": 1773076395
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi everyone,</p>\n<p>I am Ashani Dasgupta. My PhD is in Geometric Group Theory (University of Wisconsin-Milwaukee) and I am the founder of Cheenta Academy in Kolkata, India, where we work on mathematical olympiad training and research projects with school and university students. I am also a member of the Random Geometry Group at Ramakrishna Mission Vivekananda's Ancestral House, Kolkata, set up in collaboration with the Infosys-Chandrasekharan Virtual Centre for Random Geometry, TIFR.</p>\n<p>I have recently been exploring the geometry of the Lean 4 Mathlib dependency graph as an expository project for undergraduates, and Jeremy Avigad kindly suggested I introduce myself here before posting about it in general. Looking forward to engaging with this community.</p>",
        "id": 578249313,
        "sender_full_name": "Ashani Dasgupta",
        "timestamp": 1773088714
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"950805\">Martin Winter</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Newbie.20and.20chirotopes/near/578213318\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Having oriented matroids in mathlib would be great in light of the <a href=\"#narrow/channel/116395-maths/topic/Polyhedra.20in.20mathlib/with/573982556\">polyhedral theory</a> ...</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Hi <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"950805\">@Martin Winter</span> , I'm specially interested in this connection, as oriented matroids are related to some of the results I've been studying in admissible sequences of permutations. Will try to read more about it in preparation for the workshop.</p>\n<p>That being said, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"1045518\">@Jean Cardinal</span> do you have a repository somewhere with your current formalization? I'd be happy to read through the lean code to learn myself.</p>",
        "id": 617145223,
        "sender_full_name": "Nicolau Oliver",
        "timestamp": 1787044085
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Regarding matroids: are you aware of <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"329425\">@Peter Nelson</span>'s work on matroids? (I do not remember if they also worked on oriented matroids, but do remember that the design space is non-trivial, and there were some tricky trade-offs to make.)</p>",
        "id": 617152182,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1787045998
    }
